      "text": "125,451. Wait, let me check the addition again to be sure. 1,431 + 28,620 is 30,051. Then 30,051 + 95,400. 30,000 + 95,400 = 125,400. Then 51 more is 125,451. Yeah, that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, I can use another method to verify. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm. Let me try that. \n\nSo, writing it out:\n\n```\n    477\n  x 263\n  -------\n```\n\nFirst, multiply 477 by 3 (the ones place of 263):\n\n477 * 3 = 1,431\n\nThen, multiply 477 by 60 (the tens place of 263):\n\n477 * 60 = 28,620\n\nThen, multiply 477 by 200 (the hundreds place of 263):\n\n477 * 200 = 95,400\n\nNow, add them all together:\n\n1,431\n+28,620\n+95,400\n--------\n125,451\n\nYes, that matches what I got earlier. So I'm confident that the product of 477 and 263 is 125,451.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 477 and 263 is calculated by breaking down the multiplication into parts based on the place values of 263. \n\n1. Multiply 477 by 3 (ones place): 1,431\n2. Multiply 477 by 60 (tens place): 28,620\n3. Multiply 477 by 200 (hundreds place): 95,400\n\nAdding these results together: 1,431 + 28,620 + 95,400 = 125,451.\n\n**Answer:** The product of 477 and 263 is \\boxed{125451}.",
