      "index": 0,
      "text": "193 multiplied by 523, which equals 100,439.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the multiplication problem step by step.\n\n**Question:**  \nWhat is the product of **193** and **523**?\n\n---\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of **193** and **523**, we'll use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. **Multiply 193 by the units digit of 523 (which is 3):**\n   \n   \\[\n   193 \\times 3 = 579\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 193 by the tens digit of 523 (which is 2), and remember to shift one position to the left:**\n   \n   \\[\n   193 \\times 2 = 386 \\quad \\text{(Shifted one position left becomes 3860)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 193 by the hundreds digit of 523 (which is 5), and remember to shift two positions to the left:**\n   \n   \\[\n   193 \\times 5 = 965 \\quad \\text{(Shifted two positions left becomes 96500)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   579 + 3860 + 96500 = 100,439\n   \\]\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{100,\\!439}\n\\]",
