      "text": "348, 915.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **955** and **366**, we'll follow a step-by-step multiplication process.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 955 by the Ones Place of 366\nThe ones place of **366** is **6**.\n\\[\n955 \\times 6 = 5,730\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 955 by the Tens Place of 366\nThe tens place of **366** is **6**, which represents **60**.\n\\[\n955 \\times 60 = 57,300\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 955 by the Hundreds Place of 366\nThe hundreds place of **366** is **3**, which represents **300**.\n\\[\n955 \\times 300 = 286,500\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Sum All the Results\n\\[\n5,730 + 57,300 + 286,500 = 348,915\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{348,\\!915}\n\\]",
