 133,860.\n\nYes, that's consistent again. So I think the correct product is 133,860.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 970 and 138 is calculated by breaking down the multiplication into parts based on place value and then summing the results. \n\n1. Multiply 970 by 8 (ones place): 970 \u00d7 8 = 7,760.\n2. Multiply 970 by 30 (tens place): 970 \u00d7 30 = 29,100.\n3. Multiply 970 by 100 (hundreds place): 970 \u00d7 100 = 97,000.\n\nAdding these results together: 7,760 + 29,100 + 97,000 = 133,860.\n\n**Answer:** 133,860",
