st have made a mistake in the standard multiplication.\n\nWait, in the standard multiplication, I think I misaligned the digits. Let me try again.\n\n   821\n\n\u00d7 618\n\n________\n\nFirst, multiply 821 by 8: 6568\n\nThen, multiply 821 by 1 (tens place, so shift one position left): 8210\n\nThen, multiply 821 by 6 (hundreds place, shift two positions left): 492600\n\nNow, add them:\n\n   6568\n\n+ 82100\n\n+492600\n\nLet me add 6568 + 82100 first:\n\n6568 + 82100 = 88,668\n\nNow add 492,600 to 88,668:\n\n492,600 + 88,668 = 581,268\n\nWait, but using the distributive method, I got 507,378. There's a clear inconsistency here. I must have made a mistake in one of the methods.\n\nWait, let me check the standard multiplication again. Maybe I added incorrectly.\n\nWait, 821 \u00d7 618:\n\nLet me compute it step by step:\n\nFirst, 821 \u00d7 8 = 6568\n\nThen, 821 \u00d7 10 = 8210\n\nThen, 821 \u00d7 600 = 492,600\n\nNow, adding them:\n\n6568 + 8210 = 14,778\n\n14,778 + 492,600 = 507,378\n\nWait, so why did I get 581,268 earlier? Maybe I misaligned the digits when adding.\n\nWait, in the standard multiplication, when adding 6568 + 82100 + 492600, perhaps I should consider the place values correctly.\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n      6568\n\n    +82100\n\n  +492600\n\n= ?\n\nAligning the digits:\n\n     6568\n\n   +82100\n\n+492600\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n8 + 0 + 0 = 8\n\n6 + 0 + 0 = 6\n\n5 + 1 + 6 = 12 \u2192 write down 2, carryover 1\n\n6 + 2 + 2 + 1 (carryover) = 11 \u2192 write down 1, carryover 1\n\n0 + 8 + 9 + 1 (carryover) = 18 \u2192 write down 8, carryover 1\n\n0 + 0 + 4 + 1 (carryover) = 5\n\nSo the sum is 581,268.\n\nBut using the distributive method, I got 507,378. There's a contradiction. I must have made a mistake somewhere.\n\nWait, let me compute 821 \u00d7 618 using another method, perhaps breaking it down differently.\n\nCompute 821 \u00d7 618:\n\n= 821 \u00d7 (600 + 18)\n\n= 821 \u00d7 600 + 821 \u00d7 18\n\n= 492,600 + (821 \u00d7 10 + 821 \u00d7 8)\n\n= 492,600 + (8,210 + 6,568)\n\n= 492,600 + 14,778\n\n= 507,378\n\nSo this method gives 507,378, which matches my initial calculation. Therefore, the correct answer should be 507,378, and I must have made a mistake in the standard multiplication method when adding the numbers.\n\nWait, perhaps I misaligned the digits when adding. Let me try adding them again carefully.\n\n6568\n\n+82100\n\n+492600\n\nLet me write them vertically with proper alignment:\n\n      6568\n\n    +82100\n\n  +492600\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 8 + 0 + 0 = 8\n\nTens place: 6 + 0 + 0 = 6\n\nHundreds place: 5 + 1 + 6 = 12 \u2192 write 2, carryover 1\n\nThousands place: 6 + 2 + 2 + 1 (carryover) = 11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 + 8 + 9 + 1 (carryover) = 18 \u2192 write 8, carryover 1\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 + 0 + 4 + 1 (carryover) = 5\n\nSo the sum is 581,268.\n\nWait, but this contradicts the distributive method. I must have made a mistake in the standard multiplication.\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the standard multiplication steps. Let me try multiplying 821 \u00d7 618 again using the standard algorithm.\n\nFirst, write it as:\n\n      821\n\n    \u00d7618\n\n________\n\nMultiply 821 by 8: 6568\n\nMultiply 821 by 1 (tens place, so shift one position left): 8210\n\nMultiply 821 by 6 (hundreds place, shift two positions left): 492600\n\nNow, add them:\n\n   6568\n\n+ 82100\n\n+492600\n\nLet me add 6568 + 82100 first:\n\n6568 + 82100 = 88,668\n\nNow add 492,600 to 88,668:\n\n492,600 + 88,668 = 581,268\n\nWait, but this contradicts the distributive method. I must have made a mistake in the standard multiplication.\n\nWait, perhaps I'm misaligning the digits when adding. Let me try adding them again.\n\n6568\n\n+82100\n\n+492600\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n      6568\n\n    +82100\n\n  +492600\n\n= ?\n\nAligning the digits:\n\n     6568\n\n   +82100\n\n+492600\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 8 +