      "text": "764,048. \n\nWait, let me verify that addition again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. 43,248 + 720,800. Adding the thousands: 43,000 + 720,000 = 763,000. Then the remaining 248 + 0 = 248. So, 763,000 + 248 = 763,248. Hmm, that's different from what I had before. Did I miscalculate earlier?\n\nWait, I think I messed up the addition step. Let me do it more carefully. 43,248 + 720,800. Let's align them:\n\n```\n  43,248\n+720,800\n--------\n```\n\nAdding the units place: 8 + 0 = 8.\n\nTens place: 4 + 0 = 4.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 8 = 10, carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 3 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 4.\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 + 2 = 6.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 + 7 = 7.\n\nSo, putting it all together: 764,048. Okay, that matches my initial answer. So, the correct total is 764,048.\n\nI think that's it. So, the product of 901 and 848 is 764,048.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 901 and 848 is calculated by breaking down the multiplication into parts based on the place values of 848 and then summing the results.\n\n1. Multiply 901 by 8 (ones place): 901 \u00d7 8 = 7,208\n2. Multiply 901 by 40 (tens place): 901 \u00d7 40 = 36,040\n3. Multiply 901 by 800 (hundreds place): 901 \u00d7 800 = 720,800\n\nAdding these results together:\n7,208 + 36,040 + 720,800 = 764,048\n\n**Answer:** 764,048",
