it, but in the initial step-by-step, I had 4970, then 14,200, then 284,000, which adds up to 303,170.\n\nYes, that's correct.\n\nSo, the final product is 303,170.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 710 and 427 is calculated by breaking down the multiplication into parts based on the place values of 427. Multiplying 710 by each digit (7, 20, and 400) and then summing the results gives the final product.\n\nStep-by-step explanation:\n\n1. Multiply 710 by 7 (ones place of 427): 710 \u00d7 7 = 4,970\n2. Multiply 710 by 20 (tens place of 427): 710 \u00d7 20 = 14,200\n3. Multiply 710 by 400 (hundreds place of 427): 710 \u00d7 400 = 284,000\n4. Add all the results: 4,970 + 14,200 + 284,000 = 303,170\n\nAnswer: 303,170",
