      "text": "99,645.\n\nWait, let me double-check my calculations to make sure I didn't make a mistake. 195 \u00d7 500 is indeed 97,500. 195 \u00d7 10 is 1,950. 195 \u00d7 1 is 195. Adding them: 97,500 + 1,950 is 99,450. Then 99,450 + 195 is 99,645. Yeah, that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, I could use the standard multiplication method to verify. Let's write it out:\n\n```\n   195\n\u00d7 511\n--------\n```\n\nFirst, multiply 195 by 1 (ones place): 195.\n\nThen, multiply 195 by 1 (tens place), which is 1950, and shift one position to the left.\n\nThen, multiply 195 by 5 (hundreds place), which is 975, and shift two positions to the left, making it 97500.\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n```\n   195\n  1950\n+97500\n--------\n  99645\n```\n\nYes, that matches my previous result. So, the product of 195 and 511 is 99,645.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 195 and 511 is calculated by breaking down the multiplication into parts based on the place values of 511. Multiplying 195 by each digit (1, 10, and 500) and then summing the results gives the final product.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 195 by the ones place (1) of 511:**\n   \\[\n   195 \\times 1 = 195\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 195 by the tens place (10) of 511:**\n   \\[\n   195 \\times 10 = 1950\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 195 by the hundreds place (500) of 511:**\n   \\[\n   195 \\times 500 = 97500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \\[\n   195 + 1950 + 97500 = 99645\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{99645}\n\\]",
