rithm:\n\nMultiply 228 by 449.\n\nFirst, multiply 228 by 9: 2052\n\nThen, multiply 228 by 4 (tens place), which is 912, but shifted one position to the left (so it's 9120)\n\nThen, multiply 228 by 4 (hundreds place), which is 912, shifted two positions to the left (so it's 91,200)\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n2052\n+9120\n+91200\n= 102,372\n\nYes, that seems correct. So the product of 228 and 449 is 102,372.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 228 and 449 is calculated by breaking down the multiplication into parts based on place value and then summing the results.\n\n1. Multiply 228 by 9 (ones place of 449): 228 \u00d7 9 = 2052\n2. Multiply 228 by 40 (tens place of 449): 228 \u00d7 40 = 9120\n3. Multiply 228 by 400 (hundreds place of 449): 228 \u00d7 400 = 91,200\n\nNow, add all the results together:\n\n2052 + 9120 + 91,200 = 102,372\n\nSo, the final computed product is 102,372.\n\nAnswer: 102,372",
