n into 3 (ones) and 50 (tens). So maybe the correct approach is to split 979 into 900 + 70 + 9. Then multiply 172 by each part and add up the results..\n\nLet me do that step by step..\n\nFirst step: 172 multiplied by 9 (ones place). Let's calculate that:.\n\n172 × 9. Let me compute that. 170×9=1530, 2×9=18, so total is 1530+18=1548. So that's the first part..\n\nSecond step: Multiply 172 by 70 (tens place). 172 × 70. Well, 172 ×7=1204, then multiply by 10 to get 70, so 12040..\n\nThird step: Multiply 172 by 900 (hundreds place). 172 ×9=1548, then multiply by 100 to get 900, so 154800..\n\nNow, sum all three parts: 1548 + 12040 +154800..\n\nLet me add them step by step..\n\nFirst, 1548 +12040 = 13588..\n\nThen, 13588 +154800. Let's see: 13588 +154800 So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
