      "text": "97,745.\n\nWait, let me verify that addition again to be sure. 2595 + 8650 is 11,245. Then 11,245 + 86,500. Let's add 11,245 + 86,500. 11,245 + 80,000 = 91,245. Then add 6,500: 91,245 + 6,500 = 97,745. Yes, that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, I can use another method to cross-verify. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n```\n    865\n  x113\n  ----\n   2595   (865 * 3)\n  8650    (865 * 10, shifted one position to the left)\n 86500    (865 * 100, shifted two positions to the left)\n  ----\n  97745\n```\n\nAdding them up as above gives 97,745. So that's consistent.\n\nI think that's correct. So the product of 865 and 113 is 97,745.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 865 and 113 is calculated by breaking down 113 into its place values and multiplying each part by 865, then summing the results. \n\n1. Multiply 865 by 3 (ones place): 865 \u00d7 3 = 2595\n2. Multiply 865 by 10 (tens place): 865 \u00d7 10 = 8650\n3. Multiply 865 by 100 (hundreds place): 865 \u00d7 100 = 86500\n\nAdding these together: 2595 + 8650 + 86500 = 97,745\n\nSo, the final computed product is 97,745.\n\nAnswer: \\boxed{97745}",
